<task id="042" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Connector, runbooks and live E2E in Cowork and Chat</title>
    <phase>D Registration, deploy and live E2E</phase>
    <gate>after 040, 041 and 043 (043 done or cancelled)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Live end-to-end testing and runbook finalisation in the deployment phase; no code files</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Executes a fixed live test plan and finalises runbooks from 002's draft; owner runs admin steps</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>L</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Live dev-tenant work with the owner; runs alone</parallel-reason>
    <deps>040, 041, 043</deps>
    <tags>e2e-test, deploy, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-8 hours (elapsed time depends on the owner)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Re-point the 'Spaarke' connector at the dev BFF's /mcp/legal-operations, deploy the plugin package, finalise the runbooks into docs/guides/SPAARKE-COPILOT-CONNECTOR-RUNBOOK.md, and prove the full flow live in Cowork and Copilot Chat with a licensed non-admin user, plus the 20-prompt routing eval and NFR-01 latency.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in Microsoft 365 Copilot and Cowork administration and live acceptance testing.</role>
  <goal>A non-admin user resolves Work Items end to end in Cowork and in Chat (connector widget or the 043 agent) with Decision Record ids captured; routing-eval rate and NFR-01 p95s are recorded; the runbook reproduces the setup from scratch.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-16, FR-12/FR-13/FR-15 live acceptance, NFR-01, success criteria 2, 3, 4, 7, 10 and 11. Seed data: a test user with at least 200 Decide-lane Work Items across at least 3 matters, including privileged items and every lookup-bearing action type. MC1493223 gates / skills in Chat.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">docs/guides/SPAARKE-COPILOT-CONNECTOR-RUNBOOK.md (client registration, connector creation, plugin package upload and approval, user Connect)</file>
      <file role="new">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/live-e2e-results.md</file>
      <file role="new">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/routing-eval.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/drafts/connector-registration-runbook.md (from 002)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/phase0-registration-facts.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/guides/M365-COPILOT-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md (format reference)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="040" status="pending">Plugin package</dependency>
      <dependency task="041" status="pending">Dev BFF with MCP on</dependency>
      <dependency task="043" status="pending">Agent fallback, or cancelled when T1 passed</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">The owner (Global Admin) runs every admin-center step (connector re-point, plugin package approval); consent and approval behaviour is tested with a licensed non-admin user (O-20).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Live evidence saved to notes or docs contains no token, claim value or privileged record text; for the FR-04 spot-check, record only whether the marker appeared.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The runbook names only real artifacts (app registrations by display name, files by repo path) and holds no secret; each step states who runs it and whether it is scriptable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No write is attempted from the text path or by the model; completions happen only through the widget's Confirm (NFR-06).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/pcf.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/pcf/control-initialization.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/pcf/theme-management.md</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ui-test/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/dataverse-deploy/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-data-governance.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/phase0-results.md</file>
