      <file>docs/guides/M365-COPILOT-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/drafts/connector-registration-runbook.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">With the owner, re-point the 'Spaarke' connector to {devBffUrl}/mcp/legal-operations and deploy the plugin package (owner approval).</step>
    <step order="2">Verify seed data (at least 200 Decide-lane items, 3 matters, privileged items, every lookup-bearing action type).</step>
    <step order="3">Cowork: the non-admin user connects once in Settings › Sources; /spaarke-decisions renders the lane with Console-equal counts; resolve one Work Item of each lookup-bearing action type with a because rationale; capture Decision Record ids; confirm the Console shows them resolved.</step>
    <step order="4">Chat: a direct prompt 'what decisions are waiting on me in Spaarke?' calls spaarke_show_decisions; resolve one Work Item through the connector widget or, if 043 was built, @Spaarke AI; capture the id.</step>
    <step order="5">FR-04 spot-check: ask the model about the privileged item's matter; record that the marker did not appear in model text.</step>
    <step order="6">Run the 20-prompt routing eval (prompts without the skill) and record the rate in notes/routing-eval.md.</step>
    <step order="7">Measure NFR-01 on dev: 50 calls each; record p95 per tool in notes/live-e2e-results.md.</step>
    <step order="8">Finalise docs/guides/SPAARKE-COPILOT-CONNECTOR-RUNBOOK.md from 002's draft; have a second admin (or a clean re-run) follow it from scratch and record the result.</step>
    <step order="9">Run context-handoff.</step>
    <step order="10">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="11">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the widget does not render in Cowork through the plugin package, STOP and escalate with evidence (FR-16).</trigger>
    <trigger>If NFR-01 p95 misses a target, record it and escalate to the owner (targets are working assumptions, spec Assumptions) rather than changing tool behaviour here.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any live step would need a client secret or Key Vault change, STOP for human confirmation (root CLAUDE.md §9).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>docs/guides/M365-COPILOT-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md covers the April declarative agent, not a federated connector, A10 client or plugin package; no connector runbook exists (ls docs/guides | grep -i connector shows only Connection Engine docs).</existing>
    <extension>No: the April guide documents a different package type and auth plane; extending it would mix the retired 'Spaarke Copilot' agent steps with the A10 connector.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Success criterion 11 (a second admin reproduces the setup from scratch) and FR-16's runbook acceptance fail, and customer provisioning has no documented steps.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Cowork end to end">
      <url>https://m365.cloud.microsoft/cowork</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Sign in as the licensed non-admin test user</step>
        <step>Run /spaarke-decisions</step>
        <step>Verify lane counts equal the Console's Decide lane</step>
        <step>Open a Work Item, complete the wizard with a because rationale, Confirm</step>
        <step>Check the browser console for errors from the widget frame</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The Work Item leaves the lane, a Decision Record is written (id captured) and the Console shows it resolved</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Chat end to end">
      <url>https://m365.cloud.microsoft/chat</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Ask 'what decisions are waiting on me in Spaarke?'</step>
        <step>Verify spaarke_show_decisions is called</step>
        <step>Resolve one Work Item through the widget (or @Spaarke AI if 043 was built)</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>A Decision Record is written (id captured)</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Billing row in the live lane">
      <steps>
        <step>Find a billing Work Item in the lane</step>
        <step>Verify it reads 'Finding' and links to Invoice Review with no decide action</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The Invoice Review page opens for the invoice; no decision is possible in Copilot</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the host (Cowork or the local MCP Apps host) to dark theme</step>
        <step>Verify backgrounds adapt (no white surface in dark mode) and text adapts (no black text in dark mode)</step>
        <step>Verify icons use currentColor</step>
        <step>Switch back to light theme and verify the widget follows without reload</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All colours come from Fluent v9 semantic tokens driven by host context (ADR-021); nothing is stored</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands (grep, wc, git diff)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">docs/guides/SPAARKE-COPILOT-CONNECTOR-RUNBOOK.md</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/live-e2e-results.md</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/routing-eval.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A licensed non-admin user connects once in Settings › Sources and resolves one Work Item of each lookup-bearing action type in Cowork; Decision Record ids are recorded and the Console shows the items resolved (success criterion 2).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The same user resolves a Work Item in Copilot Chat through the connector widget or the 043 agent; the record id is recorded (success criterion 3).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A direct prompt without the skill invokes spaarke_show_decisions, and the 20-prompt routing-eval rate is recorded (success criterion 4).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A because rationale entered in the wizard appears on the written Decision Record (FR-15).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a billing Work Item offers only the Invoice Review link-out; the FR-04 spot-check shows no privileged marker in model text.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NFR-01 p95 over 50 calls each is recorded for show/page/plan (target 3 s), lookup (1.5 s) and complete (15 s), every call under 30 s.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">docs/guides/SPAARKE-COPILOT-CONNECTOR-RUNBOOK.md exists, holds no secret, and a second admin or clean re-run reproduced the setup from it (result recorded).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Console worklist and wizard smoke on dev passes after the live runs (success criterion 7).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>052 links the runbook from the architecture doc and doc-drift-audits it; this task authors it. Re-check Chat widget support after Ignite (17–20 Nov 2026) if Chat relied on the agent fallback.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
